IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT domain
IMPORT `g8-nouns`
IMPORT `g8-penalties`

-- g8-art29-31-information: Articles 29 to 31 of the Charities (Jersey) Law 2014: the offence of disclosing restricted information, the cases to which it does not apply,
-- the Commissioner's duty to disclose to the Comptroller and to the JFSC, and the disclosures that are permitted.
-- The offence is a prohibition (SHANT) with its penalty as data (g8-penalties); the duties of Article 30 are MUST rules; Article 31 is a list of permitted purposes,
-- a BOOLEAN over a record of the disclosure.  The consent of a person, the Comptroller's or the JFSC's requirement, and the content of Regulations under 31(f) are inputs.
-- F8.11 (which consents Article 29(1) requires) is the one fork of this module.  Information registered in a public part of the register arrives as IP25.

§ `Part 7 -- Information and enforcement`

§§ `Article 29 -- Restricted information`

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
-- 29(1): the offence
-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

§§§ `29(1) -- disclosing restricted information without consent`

-- Who is caught: a person who receives information relating to the business or other affairs of any person, (a) under or for the purposes of the Law or (b) directly or indirectly from a person
-- who has so received it.  Either route suffices to be caught.
-- src:664 | (1) Subject to paragraph (2) and to Articles 30 and 31, a person who receives information relating to the business or other affairs of any person –
-- src:665 | (a) under or for the purposes of this Law; or
-- src:666 | (b) directly or indirectly from a person who has so received it,
-- src:667 | commits an offence and is liable to imprisonment for a term of 2 years and a fine if he or she discloses the information without the consent of the person to whom it relates and (where sub-paragraph (b) applies) the person from whom it was received.
@ref Article 29(1) (src:664-666)
GIVEN info IS AN `Information received and its character` @desc What the information is and how it was received
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Art 29(1) the person received information within Article 29(1)` info MEANS
        info's `relates to the business or other affairs of a person`
    AND (   info's `received under or for the purposes of this Law`
         OR info's `received directly or indirectly from a person who so received it` )

-- F8.11.  "... if he or she discloses the information without the consent of the person to whom it relates and (where sub-paragraph (b) applies) the person from whom it was received."
-- Reading A (taken): the disclosure needs both consents - that of the person to whom it relates, and where (b) applies that of the person from whom it was received - so a disclosure lacking
-- either is an offence.  Reading B: it is an offence only if neither consent was given, so either consent suffices.  Where (b) does not apply only the consent of the person to whom it relates
-- is asked for, on both readings.
@ref Article 29(1) (src:667)
GIVEN info IS AN `Information received and its character` @desc What the information is and how it was received
      disclosure IS A `Disclosure of information` @desc The consents given
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Art 29(1) reading A: both consents given` info disclosure MEANS
        disclosure's `consent of the person to whom the information relates`
    AND (   NOT info's `received directly or indirectly from a person who so received it`
         OR disclosure's `consent of the person from whom the information was received` )

@ref Article 29(1) (src:667)
GIVEN info IS AN `Information received and its character` @desc What the information is and how it was received
      disclosure IS A `Disclosure of information` @desc The consents given
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Art 29(1) reading B: either consent given` info disclosure MEANS
    IF   info's `received directly or indirectly from a person who so received it`
    THEN disclosure's `consent of the person to whom the information relates` OR disclosure's `consent of the person from whom the information was received`
    ELSE disclosure's `consent of the person to whom the information relates`

@ref Article 29(1) (src:667)
GIVEN interp IS AN `Interpretation of Articles 26 to 36` @desc The readings of the forks of Articles 26 to 36 (F8.11 is the one read here)
      info IS AN `Information received and its character` @desc What the information is and how it was received
      disclosure IS A `Disclosure of information` @desc The consents given
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Art 29(1) the disclosure has the consent Article 29(1) requires` interp info disclosure MEANS
    CONSIDER interp's `which consents Article 29(1) requires`
    WHEN `Article 29(1) requires both consents` THEN `Art 29(1) reading A: both consents given` info disclosure
    WHEN `Article 29(1) is met by either consent` THEN `Art 29(1) reading B: either consent given` info disclosure

-- "Subject to paragraph (2) and to Articles 30 and 31": the offence is not committed where Article 29 does not apply (29(2)), where the Commissioner is required to disclose (30), or where
-- Article 31 permits the disclosure.
@ref Article 29(1) (src:664-667)
@export Whether the person commits the offence of disclosing restricted information under Article 29(1): the person received information relating to the affairs of another under or for the purposes of the Law or from someone who did, Article 29 applies to it (29(2)), the disclosure is neither required by Article 30 nor permitted by Article 31, and it lacks the consent Article 29(1) requires (default - both the consent of the person to whom it relates and, where it was received from another recipient, of the person it was received from) (2 years and a fine)
GIVEN interp IS AN `Interpretation of Articles 26 to 36` @desc The readings of the forks of Articles 26 to 36 (F8.11 is the one read here)
      `the information is registered in a public part of the register` IS A BOOLEAN @desc IP25: whether the information is registered in the public parts of the register, within the meaning of Article 10(3) to (5)
      info IS AN `Information received and its character` @desc What the information is and how it was received
      disclosure IS A `Disclosure of information` @desc The disclosure: who makes it, to whom, for what purpose, and which consents were given
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Art 29(1) the person commits an offence` interp `the information is registered in a public part of the register` info disclosure MEANS
        `Art 29(1) the person received information within Article 29(1)` info
    AND NOT `Art 29(2) this Article does not apply to the information` `the information is registered in a public part of the register` info
    AND NOT `Art 30 the disclosure is one the Commissioner must make` disclosure
    AND NOT `Art 31 the disclosure is permitted` disclosure
    AND NOT `Art 29(1) the disclosure has the consent Article 29(1) requires` interp info disclosure

-- The prohibition as it bears on this disclosure: where the offence would be committed by disclosing, the person SHANT disclose; where it would not, there is nothing prohibited.
@ref Article 29(1) (src:664-667)
@export The prohibition in Article 29(1) as it bears on a disclosure: the person must not disclose restricted information without the consent Article 29(1) requires, unless Article 29(2), 30 or 31 takes the disclosure out of the offence; FULFILLED where the disclosure would not be an offence (2 years and a fine)
GIVEN interp IS AN `Interpretation of Articles 26 to 36` @desc The readings of the forks of Articles 26 to 36 (F8.11 is the one read here)
      `the information is registered in a public part of the register` IS A BOOLEAN @desc IP25
      info IS AN `Information received and its character` @desc What the information is and how it was received
      disclosure IS A `Disclosure of information` @desc The disclosure: who makes it, to whom, for what purpose, and which consents were given
GIVETH A DEONTIC `Legal actor` `Act under Article 26 to 31`
`Art 29(1) the person must not disclose the information` interp `the information is registered in a public part of the register` info disclosure MEANS
    IF   `Art 29(1) the person commits an offence` interp `the information is registered in a public part of the register` info disclosure
    THEN PARTY `any person`
         SHANT `disclose restricted information`
         HENCE FULFILLED
         LEST BREACH BY `any person` BECAUSE "Article 29(1): the person disclosed information relating to the affairs of another without the consent the Article requires"
    ELSE FULFILLED

@ref Article 29(1) (src:667)
GIVEN interp IS AN `Interpretation of Articles 26 to 36` @desc The readings of the forks of Articles 26 to 36 (F8.11 is the one read here)
      `the information is registered in a public part of the register` IS A BOOLEAN @desc IP25
      info IS AN `Information received and its character` @desc What the information is and how it was received
      disclosure IS A `Disclosure of information` @desc The disclosure
GIVETH A MAYBE `Penalty provided`
`Art 29(1) the penalty the person is liable to` interp `the information is registered in a public part of the register` info disclosure MEANS
    IF   `Art 29(1) the person commits an offence` interp `the information is registered in a public part of the register` info disclosure
    THEN JUST `Art 29(1) the penalty provided for the offence`
    ELSE NOTHING


-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
-- 29(2): the cases to which Article 29 does not apply
-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

§§§ `29(2) -- this Article does not apply to information ...`

-- src:668 | (2) This Article does not apply to information –
-- src:669 | (a) that is registered in the public parts of the register, within the meaning of Article 10(3) to (5);
-- src:670 | (b) that at the time of the disclosure is or has already been made available to the public from other sources; or
-- src:671 | (c) in the form of a summary or collection of information so framed as not to enable information relating to any particular person to be ascertained from it.
@ref Article 29(2)(a) (src:669)
GIVEN `the information is registered in a public part of the register` IS A BOOLEAN @desc IP25: whether the information is registered in the public parts of the register, within the meaning of Article 10(3) to (5)
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Art 29(2)(a) the information is registered in the public parts of the register` `the information is registered in a public part of the register` MEANS
    `the information is registered in a public part of the register`

@ref Article 29(2)(b) (src:670)
GIVEN info IS AN `Information received and its character` @desc What the information is and how it was received
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Art 29(2)(b) the information is or has already been made available to the public from other sources` info MEANS
    info's `already made available to the public from other sources`

@ref Article 29(2)(c) (src:671)
GIVEN info IS AN `Information received and its character` @desc What the information is and how it was received
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Art 29(2)(c) the information is in a form that identifies no particular person` info MEANS
    info's `in the form of a summary or collection that identifies no particular person`

@ref Article 29(2) (src:668-671)
@export Whether Article 29 does not apply to the information: it is registered in the public parts of the register, or it is or has already been made available to the public from other sources, or it is a summary or collection from which no particular person can be identified
GIVEN `the information is registered in a public part of the register` IS A BOOLEAN @desc IP25: whether the information is registered in the public parts of the register, within the meaning of Article 10(3) to (5)
      info IS AN `Information received and its character` @desc What the information is and how it was received
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Art 29(2) this Article does not apply to the information` `the information is registered in a public part of the register` info MEANS
        `Art 29(2)(a) the information is registered in the public parts of the register` `the information is registered in a public part of the register`
    OR  `Art 29(2)(b) the information is or has already been made available to the public from other sources` info
    OR  `Art 29(2)(c) the information is in a form that identifies no particular person` info

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
-- 31: permitted disclosure (before 29(1), which is subject to it)
-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

§§ `Article 30 -- Required disclosure of information`

-- The Commissioner's duties.  Each is conditional on the recipient's requirement, which is an input; neither carries a time, so the duty stands until it is performed.
-- 31(b) and (c) are wider than these duties: the Commissioner may disclose to the Comptroller or the JFSC for any of their functions, and must disclose only for the functions named in 30.
-- src:673 | (1) The Commissioner must disclose information to the Comptroller, if required by the Comptroller for the purpose of enabling the Comptroller to discharge any of his or her functions in relation to the taxation of registered charities or other entities with any charitable purposes.
@ref Article 30(1) (src:673)
@export The Commissioner's duty to disclose information to the Comptroller, if the Comptroller requires it for the purpose of discharging functions in relation to the taxation of registered charities or other entities with any charitable purposes; FULFILLED where the Comptroller does not
GIVEN `the Comptroller requires the information for its functions in relation to the taxation of registered charities or other entities with charitable purposes` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the Comptroller requires the information for the purpose of enabling the Comptroller to discharge any of the Comptroller's functions in relation to the taxation of registered charities or other entities with any charitable purposes
GIVETH A DEONTIC `Legal actor` `Act under Article 26 to 31`
`Art 30(1) the Commissioner must disclose information to the Comptroller` `the Comptroller requires the information for its functions in relation to the taxation of registered charities or other entities with charitable purposes` MEANS
    IF   `the Comptroller requires the information for its functions in relation to the taxation of registered charities or other entities with charitable purposes`
    THEN PARTY `the Commissioner`
         MUST `disclose information to the Comptroller`
         HENCE FULFILLED
    ELSE FULFILLED

-- src:674 | (2) The Commissioner must disclose information to the JFSC, if required by the JFSC for the purpose of enabling the JFSC to discharge any of its functions under the Non-Profit Organizations (Jersey) Law 2008.
@ref Article 30(2) (src:674)
@export The Commissioner's duty to disclose information to the JFSC, if the JFSC requires it for the purpose of discharging its functions under the Non-Profit Organizations (Jersey) Law 2008; FULFILLED where the JFSC does not
GIVEN `the JFSC requires the information for its functions under the Non-Profit Organizations (Jersey) Law 2008` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the JFSC requires the information for the purpose of enabling it to discharge any of its functions under the Non-Profit Organizations (Jersey) Law 2008
GIVETH A DEONTIC `Legal actor` `Act under Article 26 to 31`
`Art 30(2) the Commissioner must disclose information to the JFSC` `the JFSC requires the information for its functions under the Non-Profit Organizations (Jersey) Law 2008` MEANS
    IF   `the JFSC requires the information for its functions under the Non-Profit Organizations (Jersey) Law 2008`
    THEN PARTY `the Commissioner`
         MUST `disclose information to the Jersey Financial Services Commission`
         HENCE FULFILLED
    ELSE FULFILLED

-- A disclosure the Commissioner is required to make: made by or for the Commissioner to the Comptroller or the JFSC, which requires it for the functions Article 30 names.
@ref Article 30 (src:673-674)
GIVEN disclosure IS A `Disclosure of information` @desc The disclosure: who makes it, to whom, and whether the recipient requires it for the functions Article 30 names
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Art 30 the disclosure is one the Commissioner must make` disclosure MEANS
        disclosure's `by or on behalf of the Commissioner`
    AND disclosure's `required by the recipient for its functions`
    AND (   disclosure's `recipient` EQUALS `a disclosure to the Comptroller`
         OR disclosure's `recipient` EQUALS `a disclosure to the Jersey Financial Services Commission` )

§§ `Article 31 -- Permitted disclosure of information`

-- Article 31 reads: "Article 29 does not preclude the disclosure of information -" and six limbs.  Each limb is a test over the record of the disclosure.
-- The endnote [4] editorial change (the words "for the purpose of" in (c)) changes no meaning; the marker stands on (f) in the consolidated text (see FRAGMENT-G8.md, contradictions).
-- src:675 | 31 Permitted disclosure of information
-- src:676 | Article 29 does not preclude the disclosure of information –
-- src:677 | (a) by or on behalf of the Commissioner, for purpose of enabling the Commissioner to discharge any of his or her functions;
@ref Article 31(a) (src:677)
GIVEN disclosure IS A `Disclosure of information` @desc The disclosure: who makes it, to whom, for what purpose
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Art 31(a) by or on behalf of the Commissioner, to enable the Commissioner to discharge a function` disclosure MEANS
        disclosure's `by or on behalf of the Commissioner`
    AND disclosure's `to enable the Commissioner to discharge a function`

-- src:678 | (b) to the Comptroller for purpose of enabling the Comptroller to discharge any of his or her functions;
@ref Article 31(b) (src:678)
GIVEN disclosure IS A `Disclosure of information` @desc The disclosure: who makes it, to whom, for what purpose
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Art 31(b) to the Comptroller, to enable the Comptroller to discharge a function` disclosure MEANS
        disclosure's `recipient` EQUALS `a disclosure to the Comptroller`
    AND disclosure's `to enable the recipient to discharge a function`

-- src:679 | (c) to the JFSC for the purpose of enabling the JFSC to discharge any of its functions;
@ref Article 31(c) (src:679)
GIVEN disclosure IS A `Disclosure of information` @desc The disclosure: who makes it, to whom, for what purpose
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Art 31(c) to the JFSC, to enable it to discharge a function` disclosure MEANS
        disclosure's `recipient` EQUALS `a disclosure to the Jersey Financial Services Commission`
    AND disclosure's `to enable the recipient to discharge a function`

-- src:680 | (d) to the Attorney General, the Bailiff or the court for the purpose of enabling them to discharge any of their functions in relation to charities, whether under this Law, a constitutional Law, the customary law, or any other law;
@ref Article 31(d) (src:680)
GIVEN disclosure IS A `Disclosure of information` @desc The disclosure: who makes it, to whom, for what purpose
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Art 31(d) to the Attorney General, the Bailiff or the court, to enable them to discharge a function in relation to charities` disclosure MEANS
        disclosure's `recipient` EQUALS `a disclosure to the Attorney General, the Bailiff or the court`
    AND disclosure's `to enable the recipient to discharge a function in relation to charities`

-- src:681 | (e) to any person for the purpose of the investigation or prosecution of any offence under any enactment or under the customary law of Jersey, or for the purpose of taking or deciding whether to take any proceedings under this Law;
@ref Article 31(e) (src:681)
GIVEN disclosure IS A `Disclosure of information` @desc The disclosure: who makes it, to whom, for what purpose
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Art 31(e) to any person, for the investigation or prosecution of an offence or for taking or deciding whether to take proceedings under this Law` disclosure MEANS
        disclosure's `for the investigation or prosecution of an offence`
    OR  disclosure's `for taking or deciding whether to take proceedings under this Law`

-- src:682 | (f) in any other circumstances prescribed by the States by Regulations.[4]
@ref Article 31(f) (src:682)
GIVEN disclosure IS A `Disclosure of information` @desc The disclosure: who makes it, to whom, for what purpose
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Art 31(f) in other circumstances prescribed by the States by Regulations` disclosure MEANS
    disclosure's `in circumstances prescribed by Regulations`

-- The States' power to prescribe the circumstances of (f).  The Regulations are not in the sources, so their content is an input: `in circumstances prescribed by Regulations`.
@ref Article 31(f) (src:682)
@export The States' power to prescribe, by Regulations, other circumstances in which restricted information may be disclosed under Article 31(f)
GIVETH A DEONTIC `Legal actor` `Act under Article 26 to 31`
`Art 31(f) the States may by Regulations prescribe other circumstances` MEANS
    PARTY `the States`
    MAY `prescribe by Regulations other circumstances of permitted disclosure`

@ref Article 31 (src:676-682)
GIVEN disclosure IS A `Disclosure of information` @desc The disclosure: who makes it, to whom, for what purpose
GIVETH A LIST OF `Provision of Article 31 that permits a disclosure`
`Art 31 the provisions that permit the disclosure` disclosure MEANS
    concat (LIST
        (IF `Art 31(a) by or on behalf of the Commissioner, to enable the Commissioner to discharge a function` disclosure THEN LIST `Article 31(a)` ELSE EMPTY),
        (IF `Art 31(b) to the Comptroller, to enable the Comptroller to discharge a function` disclosure THEN LIST `Article 31(b)` ELSE EMPTY),
        (IF `Art 31(c) to the JFSC, to enable it to discharge a function` disclosure THEN LIST `Article 31(c)` ELSE EMPTY),
        (IF `Art 31(d) to the Attorney General, the Bailiff or the court, to enable them to discharge a function in relation to charities` disclosure THEN LIST `Article 31(d)` ELSE EMPTY),
        (IF `Art 31(e) to any person, for the investigation or prosecution of an offence or for taking or deciding whether to take proceedings under this Law` disclosure THEN LIST `Article 31(e)` ELSE EMPTY),
        (IF `Art 31(f) in other circumstances prescribed by the States by Regulations` disclosure THEN LIST `Article 31(f)` ELSE EMPTY))

@ref Article 31 (src:676-682)
@export Whether Article 29 does not preclude the disclosure: it falls within one of the six limbs of Article 31 (by or for the Commissioner; to the Comptroller; to the JFSC; to the Attorney General, the Bailiff or the court; for the investigation or prosecution of an offence or proceedings under the Law; or in circumstances the States prescribe by Regulations)
GIVEN disclosure IS A `Disclosure of information` @desc The disclosure: who makes it, to whom, for what purpose
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Art 31 the disclosure is permitted` disclosure MEANS
    NOT null (`Art 31 the provisions that permit the disclosure` disclosure)
